{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560688-i-have-no-words-for-this","id":1560688,"title":"I have no words for this...","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-06-17T22:00:35-07:00","id":1560688,"title":"I have no words for this...","content":"<div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.enworld.org/threads/vampire-the-masquerade-is-getting-a-d-d-5-5e-crossover-product-coming-to-d-d-beyond-this-year.719562/\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://www.enworld.org/ewr-porta/attachments/vampire-the-masquerade-jpg.440033/\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.enworld.org/threads/vampire-the-masquerade-is-getting-a-d-d-5-5e-crossover-product-coming-to-d-d-beyond-this-year.719562/\" target=\"_blank\"> Vampire: The Masquerade is getting a D&amp;D 5.5E crossover product, coming to D&amp;D Beyond this year </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.enworld.org/threads/vampire-the-masquerade-is-getting-a-d-d-5-5e-crossover-product-coming-to-d-d-beyond-this-year.719562/\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.enworld.org/threads/vampire-the-masquerade-is-getting-a-d-d-5-5e-crossover-product-coming-to-d-d-beyond-this-year.719562/ </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> White Wolf is the latest publisher to join D&amp;D Beyond's third-party marketplace. Today, D&amp;D Beyond announced its next slate of partner content, coming out later this year. One of the new products is Vampire: The Masquerade - Bound by Blood (5.5e), a new product published by Ghostfire Gaming... </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> The world hath truly gone mad...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-17T23:35:53-07:00","id":1560690,"title":"","content":"Not sure it's really a huge shock?<br /> <br /> Hasbro made it clear they want WotC to push this on D&amp;D after the money MtG made doing crossover cards.<br /> <br /> Paradox made it clear they want to do something about their profit margins, and getting into D&amp;D Beyond is going to be an essential for any TTRPG company that doesn't want to settle for a few thousand purchased per product at best.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T00:14:58-07:00","id":1560693,"title":"","content":"Back during 3rd edition Monty Cook did a book converting the World of Darkness to the d20 system, so it's not like this is the first time. It also makes good business sense from Paradox's perspective. Getting players who are only familiar with 5E to try out WoD and then maybe move over to the official World of Darkness system could end up being profitable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T01:06:04-07:00","id":1560696,"title":"","content":"The conversion rate from d20 to other systems is likely to be minimal. Just having books in D&amp;D Beyond is going to be profitable if Hasbro achieves a fraction of what it's been talking about; since they want to bubble off as much of the TTRPG players as possible into that program.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T03:00:48-07:00","id":1560700,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560688-i-have-no-words-for-this?p=1560693#post1560693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Back during 3rd edition Monty Cook did a book converting the World of Darkness to the d20 system, so it's not like this is the first time. It also makes good business sense from Paradox's perspective. Getting players who are only familiar with 5E to try out WoD and then maybe move over to the official World of Darkness system could end up being profitable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Monty Cook WoD wasn't an adaptation, more of a licensed homage, but yeah. I have that book and I like it.<br /> <br /> Even before, 2nd Edition had official GURPS books too, so actual adaptations aren't any new either.<br /> <br /> All in all the idea isn't either surprising or bad. A lot of people already goes to great lengths to make the WoD systems work like D&amp;D because they want D&amp;D combat and mechanics, but not to admit it.<br /> <br /> There are legit reasons to switch systems in the same setting for certain games, so I'm up for this kind of adaptation. Worried about its quality, but endorse the premise.<br /> <br /> Of course, putting aside the whole subscription lock-in schema Hasbro is aiming for. That's a discussion for another thread.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T03:58:08-07:00","id":1560702,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1560688-i-have-no-words-for-this?p=1560696#post1560696\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The conversion rate from d20 to other systems is likely to be minimal.</div> </div> </div> </div>DnD and WoD (and especially VTM) are also designed for very different type of playstyle. I guess that will make it hard to get people over.<br /> <br /> I guess something like Werewolf or Mage might actually work better.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5199-aahz","name":"Aahz","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"610"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T13:03:51-07:00","id":1560715,"title":"","content":"If the OGL boom is any indication, nothing actually works better. The trend of &quot;make everything in d20!&quot; just gluts the market with d20 books and the vast majority of customers have even less reasons to try other systems because it looks like you can get anything in one you already know; regardless of how much better it might be in a different system.<br /> <br /> The issue is that learning new systems is more work than most people want to put into things over just sitting down and playing. That's part of why D&amp;D is so hard to dethrone: it was The System, and has held that position because so many people assume that's the one to start with and then never try anything else beyond D&amp;D clones like Pathfinder where you don't really need to relearn much. One of the things VtM managed to do back in the day, was get well known enough general audiences had actually heard of it and thus some people actually wanted to start with VtM/WoD over D&amp;D (something the WEG Star Wars game had previously as well) because they new at least the elevator pitch and wanted horror/urban fantasy over dungeon crawling.<br /> <br /> This is why Habro wants WotC to fill D&amp;D Beyond with adaptations of other franchises in d20 form: not only do they want people to feel sunk cost into sticking with D&amp;D because they're already paying for D&amp;D Beyond, but they want to give the impression that you don't have to look anywhere else if you want to try out other things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-06-18T13:33:01-07:00","id":1560718,"title":"","content":"Crucially, the point isn't even if D&amp;D will have all that strength or not.<br /> <br /> It is that no one will leave it because another game got adapted to it. That doesn't make any sense.<br /> <br /> An adaptation will still be D&amp;D. If the player loves it, they'll love for the D&amp;D version. If it works, it will be because translating was feasible.<br /> <br /> Even if they buy WoD books after that, will probably be to play still in D&amp;D.<br /> <br /> That would be the logic regardless, because setting and systems aren't the same thing and few people understand what makes a system stand in some situations and not others.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}